# Delphi Study Section

## Study Design

To identify relevant use cases during the implementation of this DSL, the researcher chose to proctor a Delphi study. Eligibility to participate in this study was determined by only two requirements: 

1. The participant must be over the age of 18
2. The participant must be a member of the Energy Intermarket Surveillance Group (EISG)[^1]

These eligibility requirements were introduced to both adhere to responsible research ethics[^2] and to establish a relevant baseline in the responses provided by each participant. Plainly, this helped
to ensure that the survey questions posed in this study were answered by the same individuals that might use a purpose-made DSL for energy markets. The study was conducted in two (2) rounds, where a *round*
corresponds to a list of survey-style questions that were provided to the panelists, including a mix of free-form text responses, multiple choice questions, and questions provided in a Likert format.

